! config601.dss -- OpenDSS cross-check for VoltEdge's Carson line-impedance build.
!
! Purpose: compute the IEEE 13-node Configuration 601 phase-impedance matrix FROM
! GEOMETRY (not from the published LineCode) so it can be compared apples-to-apples
! with VoltEdge's buildCarsonMatrix (api/internal/powerflow/carson.go) and with the
! published Z601. VoltEdge's TestCarsonConfig601 reproduces the published
! OFF-DIAGONAL (mutual) terms exactly, but its DIAGONAL (self) terms come out
! ~0.12+j0.03 Ohm/mile high vs the published 0.3465+j1.0179. This resolves which is
! right: if OpenDSS (fed the same geometry) also gives ~0.466, VoltEdge is correct
! and the published LineCode uses different inputs; if OpenDSS gives ~0.3465,
! VoltEdge has a self-term bug to find.
!
! Geometry is Config 601, phased B-A-C-N on the crossarm (same as the Go test):
!   phase A @ x=2.5 ft, B @ 0, C @ 7, N @ 4 ; phases h=29 ft, neutral h=25 ft.
! Conductors: phase 336,400 26/7 ACSR (GMR 0.0244 ft, Rac 0.306 ohm/mi);
!             neutral 4/0 6/1 ACSR   (GMR 0.00814 ft, Rac 0.592 ohm/mi).
!
! Run (GUI): Compile this file; read the "? Line.L601.Rmatrix/Xmatrix" echo and the
!            generated *_LineConstants.txt. Paste both matrices back for comparison.

Clear
New Circuit.cfg601 basekv=4.16 phases=3 bus1=src

! --- Conductors: GMR & radius in ft, AC resistance in ohm/mile (60 Hz) ---
! radius affects only the shunt (C) matrix, not the series Z we are checking.
New WireData.ph_336  GMRac=0.0244  GMRunits=ft  Rac=0.306  Runits=mi  radius=0.03000 radunits=ft
New WireData.ne_4_0  GMRac=0.00814 GMRunits=ft  Rac=0.592  Runits=mi  radius=0.02350 radunits=ft

! --- Config 601 geometry; reduce=yes Kron-folds the neutral into the 3x3 phase matrix ---
New LineGeometry.g601 nconds=4 nphases=3 reduce=yes
~ cond=1 wire=ph_336 x=2.5 h=29 units=ft   ! phase A
~ cond=2 wire=ph_336 x=0   h=29 units=ft   ! phase B
~ cond=3 wire=ph_336 x=7   h=29 units=ft   ! phase C
~ cond=4 wire=ne_4_0 x=4   h=25 units=ft   ! neutral (Kron-reduced)

New Line.L601 bus1=src bus2=n2 geometry=g601 length=1 units=mi

! Earth-return model + resistivity. VoltEdge uses MODIFIED CARSON at rho=100 ohm-m,
! 60 Hz. OpenDSS's default earth model is Deri -- the single most likely source of a
! self-term difference (the self earth-return term is far more earth-model-sensitive
! than the mutual, which would explain "off-diagonals match, diagonals don't"). So
! run this TWICE: once as below (carson), once with  Set earthmodel=deri  -- and note
! which, if either, reproduces the published diagonal.
Set earthmodel=carson
Set frequency=60
Set defaultbasefreq=60
Set rho=100

Solve

! Computed per-mile, Kron-reduced 3x3 phase matrices (ohm/mile), lower triangle:
? Line.L601.Rmatrix
? Line.L601.Xmatrix

! Full report -> writes <circuit>_LineConstants.txt (Zabc + sequence impedances):
Show LineConstants freq=60 units=mi rho=100
